==English==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|la|pungens}} (stem {{m|la||pungent-}}), present participle of {{m|la|pungo||to sting}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|pŭnjənt}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈpʌndʒənt/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-pungent.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Having a [[strong]] [[odor]] that [[sting]]s the nose, said especially of [[acidic]] or [[spicy]] substances.
#: ''I accidentally dropped the bottle of ammonia and after few seconds, a very '''pungent''' stench could be detected.''
#* '''1991''', [[w:Paul Chadwick|Paul Chadwick]], ''Concrete: American Christmas'', Dark Horse Books
#*: I can almost smell the fir scent… resinous, '''pungent'''.
# Having a [[strong]] [[taste]] that [[sting]]s the tongue, said especially of [[hot]] (spicy) food, which has a strong and sharp or bitter taste.
# {{lb|en|figurative}} Stinging; [[acerbic]].
#: ''The critic gave a '''pungent''' review.''
# {{lb|en|botany}} Having a [[sharp]] and [[stiff]] [[point]].

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|pungence}}
* {{l|en|pungently}}

